  "hints": [
    "Split the job in two: the cache owns the key-to-value map, and a policy object owns only the order. What four things must a policy be told about a key?",
    "Give each policy the same small interface (insert, use, forget, ranked). LRU can be an insertion-ordered map where a use is delete-then-set; LFU needs a count and a last-use stamp per key.",
    "put evicts ranked()[0] only for a new key on a full cache, and always forgets the victim in the policy too. resize is the same eviction in a loop. Look the policy up in a table by name instead of an if ladder."
  ],
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(1) per call for LRU and FIFO; this reference LFU ranks in O(n log n), and O(1) LFU exists with count buckets",
    "space": "O(capacity)"
  }
}
